<li>THCA is the raw, non-psychoactive form of the compound found in fresh cannabis. It does not get you high.</li>
<li>THC is what THCA becomes after heat is applied, through a process called decarboxylation. THC binds to CB1 receptors and produces psychoactive effects.</li>
<li>Smoking, vaping, and cooking all trigger decarboxylation. Edibles are made from pre-decarboxylated cannabis, so the conversion happens before the product reaches you.</li>
